phase=23

completed:
- phases 1-22 (see README roadmap)
- phase 23: the five remaining gaps, all implemented and tested
  - aether-cloud cloud-http feature: KubernetesProvider (in-cluster service
    account), AwsProvider (EC2 query API + own SigV4), GcpProvider (Compute +
    metadata token), AzureProvider (management API + IMDS token)
    tested against a hand-written MockServer: request shape + response parsing
  - parallel chunk transfer: Message::RegisterDataChannel / DataReady,
    Connections::send_bulk round-robins over the node's extra connections,
    NetworkTransport waits for DataReady before the task is dispatched
    agent: AgentClient::open_data_channels, shared Arc<Mutex<ChunkAssembler>>
    CLI/config: --data-channels / data_channels
  - mutual TLS: TlsConfig::with_client_ca + WebPkiClientVerifier,
    generate_ca_and_cert / issue_client_cert, agent
    connector_with_client_cert, CLI: generate-cert --with-ca,
    issue-client-cert, --tls-client-cert/--tls-client-key,
    config: tls_client_ca_path
  - WASM capabilities: WasmCapabilities { log, clock, random }, off by default;
    a module importing something not granted fails to instantiate
  - Go SDK: verified with go1.24 (vet + build clean) and run end to end
    against a live mesh; examples/hash added

test counts: 212 default / 256 with tls + cloud-http

notes:
- reqwest 0.12 (rustls-tls), hmac 0.12, sha2 0.10 - newer majors changed APIs
- rcgen needs the x509-parser feature to sign with an existing CA
- Go toolchain lives in the scratchpad (not committed): go1.24.0 windows-amd64
- cloud adapters read platform liveness only; utilisation comes from heartbeats

open work:
- run the cloud adapters against real accounts
- QUIC transport
- security review
- cost-aware cross-region scheduling
